how to start a clothing business  so i got a great question from our  youtube viewers yaseen  love you guys who wrote in to say dear  evan i'm 16 years old i'm starting my  own clothing retail businesses my  parents don't have a ton of money in me  either i wanted to ask you what i should  do  do you think i should get a job and  introduce my first collection to  investors or not  please answer me in a video please keep  doing what you do  you seen this is a great question and  i'm i'm actually glad you're open to  getting a job i have  i have two bits of advice for you the  first one is go get a job to learn the  business  okay you're 16 years old if you start  now you're probably going to make a ton  of mistakes and the easiest way to learn  is to model success learn from somebody  who's already done it  and now you may be thinking evan come on  man you're supposed to be the  entrepreneur guy you're telling me to go  get a job now how does that make any  sense  here's why it's important okay i don't  want you to go get a boring job okay i  don't want you to go work for some huge  company  where you're just getting coffee for  people and you spend two years there you  haven't learned anything  i want you to get a job to learn i want  you to go find a company  that has 10 employees that has built up  a business that you want to aspire to be  where you can be close to the  entrepreneurial founder where you can  actually learn  and make mistakes and make contacts and  understand  how the business works because  if you just start off on your own you're  going to make so many mistakes  you don't have a lot of money you're  going to burn through whatever little  money you have  and you won't achieve greatness your  chances are so low of achieving  greatness because you're going to make  so many mistakes  on your own a great model to follow is  uh is vera wang  very wing started off she was in the  fashion business and she started at  vogue  and she rose up the ranks getting  promotion after promotion after motion  at vogue  and she learned everything about the  fashion business by being  one of the editors at vogue and she made  all the contacts  and she understood what it takes when  she left vogue to start her own business  designing wedding dresses she hit the  ground running  she didn't make as many mistakes as she  would have she  had contacts she had a little bit of  money saved up right she was able to  launch his business  and make it be successful so that's  number one again you want to go find an  entrepreneur who you respect you look up  to you can learn a lot from  and work hard like be an ideal employee  don't just do what you're hired to do  you want to learn the business  right so get as close to the  entrepreneur founder as you can take on  as many projects as you can  imagine it was your own business because  soon it's going to be your own business  and you want to be able to make mistakes  while getting paid  this is like being paid to go to  university  to learn the ropes so find that company  okay the second thing is get started  okay but start  small a lot of entrepreneurs especially  in the fashion business  they see the orders right if you want to  make a deal with somebody to supply this  stuff to you whatever shirts hoodies  whatever you're making  the cost per unit is so high in small  quantities right you want to order 10  t-shirts it's going to cost you a lot of  money  you're going to lose money on those 10  shirts where  these suppliers they want you buying a  thousand five thousand  ten thousand shirts that's when the cost  per unit goes down  and you see those price breaks you think  wow okay you know what to make this  worthwhile  i gotta order five thousand shirts and  you go out  you make the order you make mistakes  because it's your first time doing it  maybe you've used the wrong you know  shirt quality  the colors don't come out great it's the  wrong pattern whatever it is you're  going to make a lot of mistakes  you spend all your money buying these 5  000 shirts  and you're stuck with 4997 of them  in your closet in your garage  wherever because you've sold three and  the rest you can't get rid of  that happens so often and you're just  stuck with all this inventory that  you've poured  all your money into the better way to go  is to start with a print on demand  service  look at zazza look at cafe press  whatever it is a t-shirt print on demand  service where you're not spending any  money  now you may be saying okay evan well  that's great but those guys make all the  profits i barely make any i may only  make a dollar a shirt  and i'm selling to those guys it doesn't  matter  because the first part of your business  here isn't to make  tons of money it's to prove your concept  what i want you to do is is go to one of  those sites  and sell 100 t-shirts sell 500 t-shirts  then you know hey this design really  takes off you may have one out of 100  designs  that really take off and then you know  okay you know what  i can afford now to go and make this one  design that's  doing awesome for us and do my own print  run  and keep all the profits for it your  chances of success  go up dramatically because you've tested  your designs  without having to spend any money on it  so one go get a job learn from somebody  in the business  who has done it who's built the ideal  company from you and get as close  to that founder as possible to learn  from them  and two start small don't go out  spending any money  put your designs on a print for demand  service  test it make sure you get some results  make sure you get some people buying  your stuff and are excited by it  before you create your first order  believe for those who watch you like the  video please click on the link that  that supports me in making these videos  below leave a comment let me know what  you think and click on my face subscribe  to the channel  thank you so much i'll see you soon

